Rankings.
In its &lt;a href="2008"&gt;2008&lt;/a&gt; edition, U.S. News &amp; World Report placed Vanderbilt at 19th, tied with the &lt;a href="University%20of%20Notre%20Dame"&gt;University of Notre Dame&lt;/a&gt;, in its ranking of national universities. In the same publication's 2007 graduate program rankings, Péabody College was listed at 3rd among schools of education, the Vanderbilt Law School was listed at 16th, the School of Medicine was listed at 18th among reséarch-oriented &lt;a href="medical%20school"&gt;medical school&lt;/a&gt;s, the School of Nursing was listed at 19th, and the Owen Graduate School of Management was listed at 34th among business schools. Additionally, Vanderbilt is ranked 1st in the nation in the fields of &lt;a href="special%20education"&gt;special education&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href="audiology"&gt;audiology&lt;/a&gt;.
